.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
World and platform contact locks with timed release\&. 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Preserves a contact point in owning-layer coordinates\&. \fBlockWorld()\fP holds a fixed point; \fBlockPlatform()\fP follows a support identified by the application\&. \fBupdate()\fP checks the supplied contact/reach policy and advances release fades in seconds\&.

.PP
The helper starts unlocked and never reacquires automatically\&. Call a lock method on a confirmed contact edge\&. \fBgetState()\fP returns an independent copy of the point, influence, and lock flag\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlockWorld()\fP, \fBlockPlatform()\fP, \fBupdate()\fP, \fBAnimation target adapters\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "AnimationContactTarget ()"

.PP
Create an unlocked contact target\&. Starts at (0, 0), with influence 0 and locked false\&. The application chooses when contact starts and whether it remains reachable\&.

.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const contact = new pdg\&.AnimationContactTarget();
contact\&.lockWorld(20, 10);
const state = contact\&.update(1 / 60, true, true);
console\&.log(state\&.x, state\&.y, state\&.influence);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlockWorld()\fP, \fBlockPlatform()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
