.SS "lockPlatform (number x, number y, number support, \fBAnimationTransform\fP frame)"

.PP
Lock a contact to a moving support\&. Converts the world point into the platform frame\&. Subsequent \fBupdate()\fP calls transform that local point using the same support's current frame\&. Replaces any previous lock and resets influence to 1\&. Singular frames throw\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP Finite contact x in owning-layer coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP Finite contact y in owning-layer coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIsupport\fP Stable nonzero integer support ID, at most Number\&.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER\&. It is an application identity, not a retained body pointer\&. 
.br
\fIframe\fP An object containing finite \fRx\fP, \fRy\fP, \fRrotation\fP (radians), \fRscaleX\fP, \fRscaleY\fP, and \fRalpha\fP (0 to 1) values\&. It maps the platform into the owning layer; both scales must be nonzero\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const frame = { x: 10, y: 0, rotation: 0, scaleX: 1, scaleY: 1, alpha: 1 };
contact\&.lockPlatform(12, 0, 1, frame);
frame\&.x = 11;
const state = contact\&.update(1 / 60, true, true, 1, frame);
// state\&.x is now 13\&.

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBupdate()\fP, \fBlockWorld()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "lockWorld (number x, number y)"

.PP
Lock a contact to a fixed world point\&. Replaces any previous lock and resets influence to 1\&. The point remains fixed until release; it does not follow platform motion\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIx\fP Finite contact x in owning-layer coordinates\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP Finite contact y in owning-layer coordinates\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlockPlatform()\fP, \fBrelease()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "release (number fadeSeconds = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Release the lock with an optional fade\&. Sets locked false immediately and preserves the last position\&. Influence falls linearly to zero as \fBupdate()\fP advances time\&. An already released target is unchanged; release does not restart its fade\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIfadeSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative fade duration in seconds; zero clears influence immediately\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
No value\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBupdate()\fP, \fBlockWorld()\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBAnimationContactState\fP update (number deltaSeconds, boolean contactActive, boolean withinReach, number support = \fR0\fP, \fBAnimationTransform\fP frame = \fRundefined\fP, number releaseSeconds = \fR0\fP)"

.PP
Follow a support or advance the release fade\&. 
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
Parameter \fRframe:\fP Required and validated only while a platform lock remains active; otherwise ignored\&.
.RE
.PP
Inactive contact, an unreachable target, or a missing/replaced platform ID releases the lock\&. World locks do not require a support\&. Released targets never reacquire automatically; call a lock method on the next contact edge\&. A zero time step preserves fade progress but can still update a platform point or release a lock\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdeltaSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative elapsed time in seconds\&. 
.br
\fIcontactActive\fP Whether the application's contact window remains active\&. 
.br
\fIwithinReach\fP Whether the application considers this contact reachable\&. 
.br
\fIsupport\fP Current support ID, or 0 when absent\&. Must be a nonnegative safe integer\&. 
.br
\fIframe\fP Current full platform transform; required only while a platform lock remains active\&. Both scales must be nonzero\&. 
.br
\fIreleaseSeconds\fP Finite nonnegative fade duration used if this update releases the lock\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
An owned contact state; see \fBanimation_contact_state\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBlockWorld()\fP, \fBlockPlatform()\fP, \fBrelease()\fP 
.RE
.PP


